# A terminal pane keeps the whole of a long build log. The pane's
# emulator is bounded by `terminal.scrollback_lines` (10000 by default,
# lines — not the emulator library's 10 KB, which is about 500 lines of
# `seq`), so the first error of a 3000-line log is still there.
#
# 3000 lines, then Shift+Home to the top of the scrollback: line 1.
command view.toggle_tree
ex term seq 1 3000; sleep 30
wait 2000
key shift+home
wait 300
expect screen contains "▌1 "
